 ],
 "literal": "Leaving behind many hills and mountains / I came, saying 'I will receive gifts and go' / To me who stood, he showed grace, and saying 'Take this / and go from here', how did he know me, / the protector hard to resist? / For this wealth given without seeing me, I am not / a trading seeker of gifts! Cherishing, / even if it is as small as a millet grain, it is sweet, if they / gave knowing the measure of their relationship.",
 "translation": "Leaving behind many hills and mountains, I came here thinking, 'I shall receive gifts and depart.' To me who stood waiting, he showed grace, and saying, 'Take this and go from here,' how did the hard-to-resist protector know my worth? For this wealth given without even seeing me, I am not a trading seeker of gifts! Even if it is as small as a millet grain, it is sweet if given with love, knowing the measure of our relationship.",
 "modern": "பல குன்றுகளையும் மலைகளையும் பின்னே விட்டுவிட்டு, 'பரிசில் பெற்றுக்கொண்டு செல்வேன்' என்று வந்தேன். அவ்வாறு நின்ற என்மீது அன்பு காட்டி, 'இதை வாங்கிக்கொண்டு இங்கிருந்து போகட்டும்' என்று என்னை எவ்வாறு அறிந்து கொண்டான் அந்தத் தாங்கற்கரிய காவலன்? என்னைக் காணாமலேயே கொடுத்த இந்தச் செல்வத்தைப் பெறுவதற்கு நான் ஒன்றும் வியாபாரப் பரிசிலன் அல்லன். அன்போடு போற்றி, தினை அளவு சிறியதாக இருந்தாலும், நம்முடைய உறவின் அளவை அறிந்து கொடுத்தால் அதுவே நமக்கு இனியதாகும்.",
 "explanation": "The poet Peruñcittiraṉār is speaking to the messengers or associates of King Atiyamāṉ Neṭumāṉ Añci, expressing his self-respect and refusal of a gift given without a personal audience. Having traveled a long distance across hills and mountains, the poet arrived expecting a warm reception and a mutual appreciation of his poetic worth. Instead, the king sent a generous gift through intermediaries without granting an audience, treating the transaction like a mere trade. The poet proudly declares that he is not a merchant of words who sells poetry for material wealth. He asserts that even a tiny gift, as small as a millet seed, is sweet and acceptable if given with personal regard and an understanding of their relationship.",
 "model": "gemini-3.5-flash",
 "generated": "2026-11-26"
}